---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const title = 'About | Find Five Letter Words';
const description =
  'How Find Five Letter Words works: a free, frequency-sorted word finder covering 2-to-20-letter words across five dictionaries.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl pt-16">
    <p class="font-monoui text-xs uppercase tracking-eyebrow">About this site</p>
    <h1 class="mt-5 text-4xl font-snug tracking-display text-balance sm:text-5xl">
      About Find Five Letter Words
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-8 text-lg">
      Find Five Letter Words is a free word finder and word-list library for puzzle players: the
      tool we wished existed every time a Wordle went to six guesses.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      The site does one thing differently from most word finders: every list is sorted by
      <em>frequency</em>, not alphabetically. Puzzle answers are almost always everyday words, so we
      rank all words by how often they appear in a trillion-word corpus of written English. The
      likely answers float to the top; the obscure tournament plays sink to the bottom, where
      Scrabble players can find them on purpose.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-snug tracking-display">Our word lists</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">
      We cover every word from 2 to 20 letters across the major game dictionaries: ENABLE (the
      public-domain list Words With Friends is built on), TWL06 (the North American Scrabble
      tournament list), SOWPODS/CSW (the international Scrabble list), and the curated Wordle answer
      pool. Offensive terms are filtered out, and each word carries its Scrabble point value. If you
      spot a missing or misplaced word,
      <a href={url('/contact/')} class="font-mid underline underline-offset-4">tell us</a>, and corrections
      will ship quickly.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-snug tracking-display">Independence</h2>
    <p class="mt-4">
      This is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to the
      New York Times, Wordle, Hasbro, Scrabble, Merriam-Webster, or Zynga. Game names are used only
      to describe what the tool is useful for. The site is free to use and supported by a small
      amount of advertising.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
